    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020135": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Specified Purpose appointment (Estimated duration: approx. 5 year post - commencing in Sept. 2026 or shortly thereafter)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Specified Purpose appointment (Estimated duration: approx. 5 year post - commencing in Sept. 2026 or shortly thereafter) Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production within the UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science Applications are invited for the post of Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production. This role, based in the UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, will support undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, research, and wider engagement in the area of dairy production. The appointee will join a dynamic and interdisciplinary team of 18 full-time academics within the Section of Animal & Crop Science, contributing to a shared mission of addressing global food, environmental, and societal challenges through teaching, research, and knowledge exchange in animal and crop production systems. We are seeking a highly motivated individual with a demonstrated passion for teaching and research in dairy production, with an emphasis on grass-based systems of production. The successful candidate will hold a PhD in Agricultural Science or a closely related discipline, with a strong focus on dairy production and ideally with research interests that intersect with grass and forage production and environmental sustainability. In addition to a strong research profile, the appointee should demonstrate excellent communication, organisational and interpersonal skills and a commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration. 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020097": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Politics and International Relations (x2), UCD School of Politics and International Relations, Permanent",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Politics and International Relations (x2), UCD School of Politics and International Relations, Permanent Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Politics and International Relations (x2) within UCD School of Politics and International Relations. The UCD School of Politics & International Relations (SPIRe) is a globally ranked, research-active school with teaching and research expertise across the fields of political science, international relations, normative political theory, international development, and other areas. It is committed to the highest standards in undergraduate and graduate teaching and research supervision. The school is home to a number of research centres, and further information can be found at: https://www.ucd.ie/spire/about/ 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 9th November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020090": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Modern Migration History, UCD School of History, Specified Purpose cover estimated duration 20 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Modern Migration History, UCD School of History, Specified Purpose cover estimated duration 20 months Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Modern Migration History within the School of History The School of History is seeking to appoint a lecturer to a 1.5 year post in modern migration History. The School has recently expanded its teaching provision and research expertise in global and migration history. The successful candidate will play a key role in developing these teaching initiatives, pursue their own research projects and act as the academic lead on the School’s Summer School. The successful candidate will be expected to be in post for the 2026/27 Spring trimester (January 2027). Salary Scale: 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) €66,055 - €104,600 Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020124": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Civil Engineering, Fixed-term post until 28 April 2028",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Civil Engineering, Fixed-term post until 28 April 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Civil Engineering. The candidate will be involved with implementing high temporal resolution sampling strategies of key parameters (and proxy/ surrogate parameters) across selected study sites that reflect a full range of catchment pressures. In addition, the successful candidate will implement approaches to assess hydromorphological condition (or changes in condition) at these selected study sites. Event based sampling, where pollution releases will be at their highest will be systematically targeted. The candidate will analyse collected data and model studied catchments to inform more rapid and better decision making in the context of a pressure-stressor-response conceptual framework that will be explored. Fixed Salary: €47,273 per annum. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 20/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020136": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Psychology, Fixed term 29th November 2029",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Psychology, Fixed term 29th November 2029 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Psychology. Applications are invited from suitably qualified candidates for a full-time, fixed term position as a Postdoctoral Researcher with the School of Psychology, in collaboration with Jigsaw-The National Centre for Youth Mental Health. This position is funded by the Health Research Board (HRB) and is available from November 2026 until November 2029. Salary Scale: Post Doc Level 1 €47,273 - €52,513 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020118": {
      "title": "Recognition Events Manager, UCD Registry Student Recruitment & Recognition Events, Permanent, Panel 12 months Permanent & Temporary posts",
      "description": "Recognition Events Manager, UCD Registry Student Recruitment & Recognition Events, Permanent, Panel 12 months Permanent & Temporary posts Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post buan Bainisteoir Imeachtaí Aitheantais laistigh de Clárlann UCD – Imeachtaí Earcaíochta agus Aitheantais Mac Léinn Cuireann Clárlann UCD réimse leathan seirbhísí riaracháin acadúla agus mac léinn ar fáil. Díríonn a misean ar sheirbhísí gairmiúla, treoir agus tacaíocht den scoth atá dírithe ar an mac léinn a fhorbairt agus a sholáthar do mhic léinn ionchasacha, do mhic léinn reatha, d’iar-mhic léinn, do bhaill foirne acadúla agus do bhaill foirne gairmiúla i ngach céim de shaolré mac léinn na hollscoile. Scála Tuarastail: €72,750 - €85,012 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 19/10/2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach. Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Recognition Events Manager within UCD Registry – Student Recruitment & Recognition Events UCD Registry delivers a broad range of student and academic administrative services, whose mission is to develop and deliver the highest quality student-centred professional services, support and advice to prospective students, current students, alumni, faculty and professional staff in respect of the key administrative functions relating to a student's life cycle in the University. Salary: 95 Admin Off Ia_2013 (2010) (7080) €72,750 - €85,012 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19/10/2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020116": {
      "title": "Research Business Development Manager, UCD School of Economics, 36 months",
      "description": "Research Business Development Manager, UCD School of Economics, 36 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Business Development Manager within UCD School of Economics. Rinn Energy is a national, co-led research centre funded by Research Ireland (Taighde Éireann), bringing together a consortium of leading universities and partners to deliver internationally leading, interdisciplinary research to support the transition to a low-carbon, secure, and resilient energy system. The Centre seeks to appoint a Business Development Manager (BDM) to successfully build collaborative research relationships between our world-leading academics and industry. The role requires identifying new industry members, projects, and training opportunities while maintaining a significant understanding of academic capabilities and industry requirements. The successful candidate will develop a portfolio of fully funded and co-funded collaborative research projects, with success measured directly by increased industry investment in the centre. Salary Scale: €88,000 - €105,000 per annum. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020119": {
      "title": "Research Project Manager, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, 12 months (Temporary, Part-Time @ 0.5fte)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Research Project Manager, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, 12 months (Temporary, Part-Time @ 0.5fte) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Project Manager within UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science. The EVEREST project is a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Staff Exchange (MSCA SE) funded under Horizon Europe, focused on cutting-edge research into extracellular vesicles (EVs) for innovative diagnostic and therapeutic applications in oncology, cardiovascular, and neurodegenerative diseases. The Research Project Manager will play a key role in managing the project across its multiple partners in multiple countries, supporting the coordination of up to 285 months of secondments between academic and non-academic institutions. Salary: €40,000 - €50,000 per annum (€20,000 - €25,000 per annum pro rata) Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020131": {
      "title": "Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Physiotherapy, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy & Sports Sciences, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Part-Time 0.5FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Physiotherapy, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy & Sports Sciences, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Part-Time 0.5FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Physiotherapy within the School of Public Health Supporting the UCD Director of Clinical Education, Subject Head, Programme Director(s) and Practice Education Team to deliver high quality academic and practice placement education. This position is aligned with Physiotherapy . The Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor will support staff on practice placement sites and the UCD Practice Education Team to deliver high quality practice placement education. The Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor will also be available to support students virtually and/or in person if required by the UCD Practice Education Team. The appointee will contribute to module coordination and delivery for programmes offered by the school on-site in UCD and/or on-line where appropriate. The role will be based on site in UCD and/or on practice placement sites as directed by their line manager, with travel as required. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum Pro Rata @ 0.5 FTE Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020120": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow in Environmental Policy, UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Temporary 5 years, Part-time (0.8 FTE), (Commencing on or before 01 January 2027)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Teaching Fellow in Environmental Policy, UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Temporary 5 years, Part-time (0.8 FTE), (Commencing on or before 01 January 2027) Applications are invited for a temporary part-time (0.8 FTE) post of a Teaching Fellow in Environmental Policy within UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy. The successful candidate will play a key role in the delivery and development of Environmental Policy teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate level, working across the Environmental Policy degree programmes to support high-quality, research-informed, policy-oriented, and experiential learning. The Teaching Fellow will contribute to the design, delivery and assessment of Environmental Policy modules, including through lectures, workshops, tutorials, project-based learning and other forms of skills-based teaching. In addition to the teaching duties, a particular focus of the role will be supporting module coordinators on modules with substantial student numbers, including teaching, administration and assessment of the modules. Overall, the Teaching Fellow will be expected to contribute to continuity of teaching provision across the Environmental Policy subject area. The post will have significant responsibilities in programme and student support, including module management, programme administration, management of online platforms, external-examiner support, supervision of postgraduate internships and research projects, as well as contributing to programme activities including orientation, careers and employer engagement. Fixed Salary: €49,500 Per Annum Pro-Rata (i.e. equal to €39,600 Per Annum, Part-time at 0.8 FTE) Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020059": {
      "title": "UCD Post doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, Temporary 3 years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/10/2026 UCD Post doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, Temporary 3 years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science Applications are invited for a very dynamic post-doctoral scientist to lead our Precision Nutrition, Obesity and Cancer Project within the Precision Oncology Ireland Programme (POI; https://www.precisiononcology.ie/) with Prof Helen Roche’s Nutrigenomics Team at UCD Conway Institute https://people.ucd.ie/helen.roche; in collaboration with Dr Martina Wallace and Dr Fiona McGillicdddy. POI, now in its second phase POI2, is a pioneering Irish consortium that brings together Irish universities, cancer charities, industry partners and healthcare providers to advance personalised cancer treatment. Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 09-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020110": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biomolecular & Biomedical Science, Temporary 24 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biomolecular & Biomedical Science, Temporary 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Biomolecular & Biomedical Science. Applications are invited for a temporary, full-time position of Post-Doctoral Researcher in the UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, based in the Conway Institute. The lab is also linked with the FutureNeuro Research Centre (https://www.futureneurocentre.ie/). The successful applicant will work on a two-year research project exploring translational disruptions in mouse models of epilepsy. The postdoctoral researcher will use a combination of pharmacological and transgenic approaches, in vivo mouse models of epilepsy and molecular-based analyses to determine how altered translation contributes to epileptogenesis and seizure disorders. There will also be the opportunity for the researcher to explore and profile novel epitranscriptomic modifications in epilepsy. Examples of previous work can be found here: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=d2vwSvIAAAAJ&hl=en Fixed Salary: €47,273 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020048": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Researcher Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, Temporary 18-month",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Researcher Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, Temporary 18-month Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Researcher Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science. The Chromatin Mechanisms in Disease laboratory (https://conwaychromatinlab.com/) at University College Dublin, led by Dr. Eric Conway, are recruiting a postdoctoral fellow to work on understanding the mechanisms through which the repressive histone modification H2AK119ub1 is dysregulated in disease. This position will be funded through a Wellcome Trust award. Histone H2A lysine 119 mono-ubiquitination (H2AK119ub1) is a repressive histone modification that is catalysed by the PRC1 complex and erased by the PR-DUB complex. Variants in critical subunits of each complex are known to be the causative event in diverse human diseases, such as AML and chromatinopathies. This project will investigate how pathogenic variants in members of the PRC1 and PR-DUB complexes contribute to changes in H2AK119ub1 using cancer and neurodevelopmental disease model systems. This will encompass a range of functional genomics, biochemistry and proteomics methods to investigate the precise impact that variants have on PR-DUB and PRC1 function – using methods such as CUT&Tag, Captify, RNA-seq, immunoprecipitation followed by mass spectrometry and high throughput pooled CRISPR screens. The role of the applicant will be either computational biology, wet-lab or a hybrid of both depending on the successful candidates expertise. There will be strong opportunities for continued professional development as part of UCD Research Careers Framework and through attendance at external training courses and conferences. The applicant will be strongly encouraged and supported to pursue external funding opportunities during the period of the appointment in line with the development of their own career prospects and to further the overall research activities of the group. PD1 Salary: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum PD2 Salary: €55,399 - €60,250 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers who have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020138": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering, UCD School of Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering, Permanent",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/12/2026 Associate Professor in Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering, UCD School of Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering, Permanent Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Associate Professor in Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering within UCD School of Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering The UCD School of Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering invites applications for the position of Associate Professor in Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering. The successful candidate will provide academic and research leadership, maintain and further develop an internationally recognised programme of research, attract competitive external funding, and supervise doctoral and postdoctoral researchers. They will contribute to high-quality teaching and project supervision at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including core subjects in the professionally accredited BE/ME programmes, and will play a substantive role in curriculum development, academic administration and School leadership. Research should complement or strengthen one or more of the School's priority areas: Pharmaceutical/Biopharmaceutical Engineering, Energy and the Environment, or Advanced Materials Engineering. The appointee will be expected to enhance the School's international profile and contribute to its academic, professional and wider societal impact. Application requirements: When preparing an application for this post, applicants should submit: A cover letter (no longer than three pages), A curriculum vitae and a list of publications. The cover letter should outline how the candidate meets the selection criteria and set out a forward-looking vision for their contribution at UCD, including their proposed research programme and external funding strategy, educational contribution, and approach to academic leadership. Where possible, applicants should include their ORCID. 95 Associate Professor_2010 Salary Scale: €85,864 - €121,260 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 11-Dec-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020154": {
      "title": "Data Scientist II, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR, Temporary 12 months post - with the possibility of Extension",
      "description": "Closing Date: 21/10/2026 Data Scientist II, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR, Temporary 12 months post - with the possibility of Extension Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Data Scientist II within UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR. CeADAR is funded by the Irish government via Enterprise Ireland and the IDA and is based in University College Dublin. As the national centre for applied artificial intelligence, CeADAR’s mission is to help industry and the public sector to adopt AI. In addition, CeADAR is also the designated European Digital Innovation Hub for AI in Ireland, and has a strong presence in the European RD&I landscape. See www.ceadar.ie for further details. Salary Range: €55,000 - €70,000 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 21st October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020143": {
      "title": "Dispensary Veterinary Nurse, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Plus 12 Month Temporary Panel)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Dispensary Veterinary Nurse, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Plus 12 Month Temporary Panel) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Dispensary Veterinary Nurse within UCD School of Veterinary Medicine. UCD Veterinary Hospital (UCDVH) is seeking to appoint a veterinary nurse (career grade) (core) as part of the Dispensary Unit to provide a high standard of nursing care working within the team, fulfilling dispensary, prescription and stock requirements for hospital services. Particular to this position: You will be required to work 36.5 hours per week over 5 days during the week between Monday and Sunday. Weekend and weekday out-of-hours working may be required on a rota basis. Start and finish times will vary depending on the needs of the Hospital. The actual allocation of these hours of work will be arranged with your line manager. Vet Nurse_Career Grad (7928) Salary Scale: €38,255 - €49,021 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Altra Tréidliachta laistigh de Scoil an Leighis Tréidliachta UCD. Tá Ospidéal Tréidliachta UCD (UCDVH) ag iarraidh altra tréidliachta (grád gairme) (croílár) a cheapadh mar chuid den Aonad Íoclainne chun ardchaighdeán cúraim altranais a sholáthar ag obair laistigh den fhoireann, ag comhlíonadh riachtanais íoclainne, oidis agus stoic do sheirbhísí ospidéil. Go háirithe leis an seasamh seo: Beidh ort 36.5 uair a chloig a oibriú in aghaidh na seachtaine thar 5 lá i rith na seachtaine idir Dé Luain agus Dé Domhnaigh. D’fhéadfadh go mbeadh gá le deireadh seachtaine agus le hobair lasmuigh d’uaireanta oibre i rith na seachtaine ar bhonn róta. Beidh amanna tosaithe agus críochnaithe éagsúil ag brath ar riachtanais an Ospidéil. Socrófar leithdháileadh iarbhír na n-uaireanta oibre seo le do bhainisteoir líne. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 23 Mí Deireadh Fomhair 2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020141": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Crop Science, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Temporary Fixed Term 3 year contract or Permanent post",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Crop Science, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Temporary Fixed Term 3 year contract or Permanent post Applications are invited for a temporary or permanent post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Crop Science within UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science The appointee will join the Animal and Crop Science Section and will contribute to both undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, conduct high quality research in Crop Science and engage in associated administrative tasks. The appointee will join a highly motivated and research active Crop Science team who are involved with teaching and research in areas including principles of crop science, cereal production, root and alternative crops, grassland, plant health, organic agriculture, digital agriculture and bioenergy. 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020145": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Veterinary Physiology and Equine Internal Medicine, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 1 Year (Part-Time 0.4 FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Veterinary Physiology and Equine Internal Medicine, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 1 Year (Part-Time 0.4 FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Veterinary Physiology and Equine Internal Medicine within the School of Veterinary Medicine. This is a temporary post as Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Veterinary Physiology (0.2FTE) and Equine Internal Medicine (0.2FTE) based in the School of Veterinary Medicine, UCD. This split post sits within the Sections of “Veterinary Biosciences” and “Equine Clinical Studies, Diagnostic Imaging and Anaesthesia”, and the appointee will be expected to significantly enhance the existing team within both sections. Applicants must be in possession of a degree in veterinary medicine registrable with the Veterinary Council of Ireland (www.vci.ie) 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 – €104,600 per annum Pro Rata @ 0.4FTE Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information, please follow the link: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020152": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Architecture, Planning & Environmental Policy, Temporary 36 months post",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Architecture, Planning & Environmental Policy, Temporary 36 months post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within the School of Architecture A 36-month post-doctoral position is available in the UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy in the area of rural planning, rural development, local regeneration and demographic changes. ‘REROOTED’ (Resilient European rural outlooks: opportunities for transformation, empowerment and development) is a Horizon Europe funded project involving an international collaboration involving universities from Ireland, the Netherlands, Italy, Denmark, Greece and Estonia, along with partners in practice, to examine rural demographic changes and strategies for rural regeneration. The project is interdisciplinary, comprising research methods spanning quantitative and qualitative approaches. Specifically, this post-doctoral position will assist with project workpackages related to (1) understanding driving forces and impacts of rural demographic trends; (2) evaluating national and regional strategies for addressing demographic changes; and (3) exploring local innovation strategies. This work will also involve primary research based in rural Ireland and collaborating closely with local groups. The appointed person will be responsible for key deliverables, data gathering and analysis, report writing and project dissemination. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. PD1 Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 per annum PD2 Salary Range: €55,399 - €56,957 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020156": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or Level 2, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 24 months",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or Level 2, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or Level 2 within UCD School of Earth Sciences. This postdoctoral position is part of the ROTTnROCK project, funded by a European Research Council Synergy grant (http://rottnrock.org). Candidates with expertise in numerical modelling, particularly Finite Element Method modelling, and thermal or fluid coupling are encouraged to apply. The position will be funded for 24 months, with opportunity for extension. Funding will also be supplied for computing, fieldwork, attendance at conferences and workshops, and publication fees. PD1 Salary: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum ; PD2 Salary Scale : €55,399 - €60,250 Per Annum** Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 04/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020153": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD Mathematics and Statistics, Temporary 24 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD Mathematics and Statistics, Temporary 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within the School of Mathematics and Statistics We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher to join the School of Mathematics and Statistics at University College Dublin (UCD). The position is funded by the Centre for Artificial Intelligence in Weather Forecasting and Climate Change, a collaboration between UCD and Met Éireann. The postdoctoral researcher will be co supervised by meteorologists from Met Éireann’s Research and Application Division. The successful candidate will contribute to cutting edge research focused on the statistical post processing of raw numerical weather prediction (NWP) output to correct known model biases. Bias corrected output will provide more accurate forecasts, delivering significant downstream benefits for forecasters and for applications that rely on NWP output. The project is therefore central to a wide range of weather-related services provided by Met Éireann. It will contribute to improving the accuracy and reliability of forecasts delivered through Met Éireann’s website and app, third party services, and weather warnings, and aligns closely with Met Éireann’s overall strategy. Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020148": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Temporary 18 months post",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Temporary 18 months post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Postdoctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering. NanoMind-GenAI is an ARC-ICT funded project on the development of a AI driven formulation and manufacturing software platform for lipid nanoparticles with the applications towards RNA therapeutics. NanoMind-GenAI will deliver an AI-driven decision-support platform that closes this gap. Combining agent-supported literature retrieval and interpretation with machine learning validated on over 3,000 LNP formulations, the platform will generate explainable, evidence-based formulation recommendations, supporting faster and more knowledge-grounded candidate prioritisation with traceable reasoning. Expected outputs include a tested software workflow, evidence-based candidate prioritisation methods, research publications and contributions to the project’s commercial development. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. Salary range: €47,273 - €49,890 per annum. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020139": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Music, 18 months",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Music, 18 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Music. The School of Music at University College Dublin is launching a new postdoctoral fellowship competition for outstanding early-career researchers working in any area of music research. The scheme is intended to provide career development opportunities for leading music researchers at an early stage of their careers while further enriching the lively research culture of the School. This post runs alongside our existing commitment to – and success in – supporting candidates for externally-funded schemes such as Government of Ireland and MSCA Postdoctoral Fellowships. The Fellowship will last 18 months and will provide extensive research time and support; successful candidates will also have the opportunity to gain teaching experience. The fellowship will start on 01 January 2027. Salary: €47,273 per annum . Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 01/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020146": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in Remote Sensing of Peatlands, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 7 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Research Assistant in Remote Sensing of Peatlands, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 7 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant in Remote Sensing of Peatlands within UCD School of Earth Sciences. Applications are invited from suitably qualified persons for the post of Research Assistant in Remote Sensing of Peatlands at University College Dublin (UCD). The post will be based at the Irish Centre for Research in Applied Geosciences (iCRAG), which is hosted at UCD School of Earth Sciences. The post will involve extensive collaboration with colleagues within iCRAG and at CeADAR, the national centre for applied data analytics and Artificial Intelligence. Research Assistant Salary Scale: €34,129 - €43,227 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020142": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, School of Earth Sciences, 2 years until maximum 31st December 2028",
      "description": "Research Assistant, School of Earth Sciences, 2 years until maximum 31st December 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within School of Earth Sciences . The Research Assistant will be primarily responsible for the day to day running of (1) a Bruker M4 Tornado+ microXRF machine for analysis of thin section, core and hand samples, and (2) our Multi Sensor Core Logger instrument, a Geotek MSCL-S which scans various sizes of drill core: this will be installed in Q4 2026. You will contribute to data collection across several projects in economic geology and raw materials in the School. In addition, the post holder will contribute to geothermal projects, acquiring and preparing representative core and rock samples from typical geological regions in Ireland, characterising their thermo-hydraulic properties, and supporting the School’s petrographic laboratories. The role involves fieldwork at sites and core stores across the Republic of Ireland, and the successful candidate must be willing to travel and to work in the field as required. This position will be a key part of the large team working on sedimentary basin research in Ireland and globally in the School of Earth Sciences. Research Assistant Salary: €34,129 - €38,102 per annum (Research Assistant points 1 – 6) Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 03/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020150": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary 9 months (Part-Time 0.5FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Research Assistant, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary 9 months (Part-Time 0.5FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within UCD School of Medicine. Applications are invited for a research assistant to support the ECHO study, a prospective observational cohort examining childhood health outcomes following maternal e-cigarette use. The study follows mothers and their babies from pregnancy to two years of age and examines growth, respiratory and neurobehavioural development. The impact of vaping during pregnancy on childhood health outcomes is currently unknown and this is the first study in the world to ever examine these outcomes longitudinally over the first two years of life. Salary Range: €34,129 - €36,272 Per Annum Pro Rata @ 0.5 FTE. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020103": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems, Temporary Fixed Term 6 Months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Research Assistant, UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems, Temporary Fixed Term 6 Months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within the School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems, is currently seeking to appoint a highly motivated research assistant to contribute to a funded project titled End of Life care in Nursing Homes The successful candidate will play a crucial role the experience of staff providing end-of-life care in nursing homes, particularly focusing on the development and deployment data collection tools, support with data analysis, creation of publications, and development of conference presentations. Salary Range: €34,129 - €35,395 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020151": {
      "title": "Research Project Manager, UCD School of Geography, 36 months (Temporary part time)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Research Project Manager, UCD School of Geography, 36 months (Temporary part time) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Project Manager within UCD School of Geography. The Research Project Manager will specifically support two recently awarded European Research Council (ERC) Grant awardees, projects MigHealthGaps, and HERDPATH. The position is part-time at 50% and provides the opportunity for a suitable candidate to gain valuable experience working in UCD supporting two research leaders in all aspects of ERC research management and administration. Salary: €47,489 (@0.51282 fte pro rata) Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020149": {
      "title": "Robotics Research Engineer, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Temporary 12 months post",
      "description": "Robotics Research Engineer, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Temporary 12 months post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Robotics Research Engineer within UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering Funded by Horizon Europe’s European Innovation Council Patherfinder programme, the CEREBRIS project aims to revolutionise how neurological conditions are monitored and managed. By combining brain signals, imaging, movement and clinical data, CEREBRIS aims to support earlier diagnosis, more precise prognosis to transform personalised care. Salary: €38,000 - €48,000 annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27-10-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020159": {
      "title": "Special Lecturer / Clinical Tutor in Neonatology (The National Maternity Hospital), UCD School of Medicine / National Maternity Hospital, Temporary Fixed Term 12 months from 12th July 2027 to 9th July 2028",
      "description": "Special Lecturer / Clinical Tutor in Neonatology (The National Maternity Hospital), UCD School of Medicine / National Maternity Hospital, Temporary Fixed Term 12 months from 12th July 2027 to 9th July 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Special Lecturer / Clinical Tutor in Neonatology (The National Maternity Hospital) within UCD School of Medicine / National Maternity Hospital. The Special Lecturers/Clinical Tutors play a major role in supporting, organizing and delivering clinical teaching for our students on rotation in our affiliated Teaching hospitals. The Clinical Tutors instruct and supervise students during their clinical attachment, provide lectures and tutorials as part of the formal clinical curriculum and assist with the preparation of clinical examinations. They provide academic support and career mentoring to students and ensure that the clinical rotation supports the learning objective of the relevant module. A number of Clinical Tutors are also actively involved in our biomedical, clinical or medical education research working with a specific Principal Investigator and may be undertaking a higher research degree (e.g. MD, MCh, MAO, MSc or PhD). These individuals are responsible for undertaking research experiments or data reviews and disseminating their findings through publication as a thesis, in academic journals or at scientific meetings. All Clinical Tutors are part of a vibrant community of academic staff who pass on their clinical experience and expertise to the next generation of medical professionals. The School provides academic support and training such that the Tutors themselves develop their own educational expertise and leadership. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum. Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 29/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020163": {
      "title": "Special Lecturer Clinical Tutor in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, The National Maternity Hospital, UCD School of Medicine National Maternity Hospital, Temporary Fixed Term 12 months from 12th July 2027 to 9th July 2028",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Special Lecturer Clinical Tutor in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, The National Maternity Hospital, UCD School of Medicine National Maternity Hospital, Temporary Fixed Term 12 months from 12th July 2027 to 9th July 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Special Lecturer Clinical Tutor in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, The National Maternity Hospital within UCD School of Medicine / National Maternity Hospital The Special Lecturers/Clinical Tutors play a major role in supporting, organizing and delivering clinical teaching for our students on rotation in our affiliated Teaching hospitals. The Clinical Tutors instruct and supervise students during their clinical attachment, provide lectures and tutorials as part of the formal clinical curriculum and assist with the preparation of clinical examinations. They provide academic support and career mentoring to students and ensure that the clinical rotation supports the learning objective of the relevant module. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 30-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020147": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Medicine/Systems Biology Ireland, Temporary 1 year",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Medicine/Systems Biology Ireland, Temporary 1 year Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Medicine/Systems Biology Ireland. Applications are invited for a Postdoctoral Research Fellow position to support a programme of work on early onset colorectal cancer. Based within the Research Groups of Dr Oleksii Rukhlenko and Prof. David Gomez Matallanas in Systems Biology Ireland (SBI) at UCD, the Postdoctoral Research Fellow will contribute to the ambitious Precision Oncology Ireland 2 (POI-2) Programme, which is coordinated by SBI and brings together researchers across multiple institutions. The role requires (1) knowledge of bioinformatics, (2) extensive hands-on experience in analysis of omics data, (3) some practical experience in multi-omics integration and network biology, (4) understanding of cancer biology and systems biology. About the Precision Oncology Ireland Programme: Precision Oncology Ireland (POI; https://www.precisiononcology.ie/) is a pioneering Irish consortium that brings together Irish universities, cancer charities, industry partners and healthcare providers to advance personalised cancer treatment. Coordinated by Systems Biology Ireland at UCD, POI leverages systems biology approaches to analyse complex molecular data and understand cancer at a deeper level. By integrating multiomics data, imaging, and clinical data through computational modelling, the consortium aims to tailor therapies to individual patients' tumour profiles. POI is working to improve diagnostics, reduce unnecessary treatments, and accelerate the development of targeted cancer therapies. PD1 Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. PD2 Fixed Salary: €55,399 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers who have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020155": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 3 years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 3 years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Veterinary Medicine UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, in association with UCD School of Mathematics and Statistics, is advertising an exciting research position as part of a cross-border project using epidemiological modelling to inform sustainable control of bovine tuberculosis on the Island of Ireland. The Post-doctoral Research Fellow will develop and implement mechanistic and statistical modelling tools, tapping the experience of a strongly interdisciplinary research team, to better target interventions to control tuberculosis in Irish cattle. Post-doctoral level 1 or 2 Salary Scale: €47,273 – €53,925 per annum or €55,399 - €60,250 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 11-Nov-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020161": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Medicine - Charles Institute of Dermatology, Temporary 36 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Medicine - Charles Institute of Dermatology, Temporary 36 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Medicine - Charles Institute of Dermatology. The ECM lab led by Associate Professor Seungkuk Ahn at University College Dublin in Ireland has an opening for a Postdoctoral Research position (PD level 1) to work on the ERC-funded “DESIGN-ECM” project to investigate the role of species and sex of extracellular matrix and cells for better designing 3D tissue models. Human mimetic preclinical models imitate human organs, tissues, and diseases to enable safer, more accurate testing for new drugs and therapies. Such models are created by employing core biomaterials and cells existing in our tissues. These models have significant potential to enhance our understanding of human disease and the development of treatments. However, the majority of human preclinical models to date have neglected the species and sex of the extra cellular matrix and cells as biological variables, while species- and sex-dependent biomaterial and cell properties have been well acknowledged in animal and clinical studies. Led by Dr Seungkuk Ahn, DESIGN-ECM will address this gap by investigating species-driven dimorphism in biomaterials and cell biology across various disciplines such as materials science, bioengineering, organoids, mechanobiology, nanobiotechnology. Success in this project will reshape the design of future preclinical models to seriously reckon with species and sex of biomaterials and cells, moving towards personalised tissue models in the long term. Candidates will work together with 2 PhD students to establish the core methodologies and data sets for the first 36 months of the total 60-month ERC project. The main scientific works will 1) engineer and characterise 3D ECM scaffolds, 2) perform in vitro cell validations, and 3) develop 3D ovarian organoid models. The start date of this position is 01 May 2027. Fixed Salary: €47,273 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 05 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020157": {
      "title": "Work Ready Graduate Data Scientist x 12, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR Ireland’s Centre for Applied AI, Temporary 12-month post(s)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 28/10/2026 Work Ready Graduate Data Scientist x 12, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR Ireland’s Centre for Applied AI, Temporary 12-month post(s) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Work Ready Graduate Data Scientist x 12 within the School of Computer Science Are you interested in becoming an applied AI/data scientist and developing a career in the world’s fastest growing and arguably most exciting discipline of AI/data analytics? Then this ‘work-ready’ graduate training programme may be a great opportunity for you. CeADAR Ireland’s Centre for Applied AI is running the next phase of the Work Ready Graduate Programme for 2027 from January 2027 to December 2027. Work Ready Trainee Graduates are hosted both at CeADAR and at one of our industry partners offices. CeADAR is recruiting 12 Work Ready Graduate candidates with solid coding experience and with a postgraduate degree in a numerate subject such as Computer Science, Data Analytics, AI, Engineering or Maths/Statistics. Eligible candidates must hold a completed Master’s qualification from a university or accredited higher education institution. CeADAR, based in University College Dublin, is funded by Enterprise Ireland to support companies in embracing and leveraging AI technology. CeADAR is also the designated European Digital Innovation Hub for AI in Ireland. The applied research at CeADAR covers broad aspects of AI and data analytics using advanced machine learning to deal with structured and unstructured data coming from many different sectors. This is an exciting opportunity to be involved in this strategic and nationally important area of AI where CeADAR is shaping the strategy at the national and EU level. Fixed Salary: €38,885 per annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 28 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    }
  },
